      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To the otolaryngologist, there are multiple causes for head or facial pain: headaches due to ear diseases; idiopathic neuralgias; \"referred otalgia\" involving cranial nerves V, IX, X; temporomandibular joint dysfunction; rhinological pathologies, including post-traumatic trigeminal neuralgia; \"facial sympathalgias\"; the styloid process syndrome; and cervical spine problems. Less known causes of head and neck pain are stressed, and emphasis placed on their diagnosis and treatment."},
